{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/753855-so-how-much-experience-do-you-folks-have-with-werewolf","id":753855,"title":"So, how much experience do you folks have with Werewolf?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-04T06:34:56-08:00","id":753855,"title":"So, how much experience do you folks have with Werewolf?","content":"How much have you folks done with Werewolf? I'd love to hear how much experience you've had and what kind of games you've been running/playing in.<br /> <br /> I've been running Werewolf in some form since 1999. I I live in a country where it is nigh impossible to buy RPG books in 2015, in 1999 I was stuck with loaning and photocopying stuff and binging on usenet for extra information. My first proper book was Revised which I literally had to wheedlee and cajole a guy into getting for me through Amazon. My experience as a player sucks, though. I have managed to persuade a couple of folks to run one shots in my campaigns so I maybe collected 5-6 sessions as a player in the past 16 years. As a storyteller, though...<br /> <br /> I've started with a premade adventure from White Wolf magazine that was on the old White Wolf site. It was pretty simplistic and downright dungeon-crawly and I remember modifying it quite a bit even then to add some color. I would continue to run that same thing in different iterations 3-4 times for oneshots and Werewolf demos. There were a number of false starts, and my group never properly bit until...<br /> <br /> Rage Accross Egypt. I found this thing in a bin in a Comic book store. It was horribly overpriced and at the time the only comic book shop in the country was actually trying to be hip so they ordered random RPG books and offered them in store at huge markups (i paid like 40$ for Rage Across Egypt!). The book was amazing and inspiring and it really got me aching for a game, and I've been wanting to run a Werewolf game for a while. So i gathered my best friends, and persuaded them to pick up Werewolf. What we ended up playing was a two year chronicle about the adventures of a pack of Scottish Fianna and their Get alpha and how they had to leave their sept due to causing havoc with an opposing pact and decided to head to Egypt and join the Crusade of Buries the Dead. The merry band proceeded to fight Setites, pass through all the Umbras of Egypt on a glorious spirit quest, rescued the Bubasti kinfolk and fought the Brain Eaters of Cairo...<br /> <br /> My second game was inspired by Rage Accross Russia. I had to dump most of that book, due to it being horribly bad in a very early 90s game written by someone who never bothered to research different parts of the world properly, but the Zmei, and Baba Yaga's armies sounded intriguing. That game would be defined by a single thing that totally changed the original concept - a player wanted a Wendigo. It totally didn't fit, until it dawned on me. I allowed it and told a tale of two Carns that exchange cubs every generation as a part of a pact of peace between the Wyrmcomers and the Native Garou. The pack was led by a mighty Get Ahroun who tried to walk in the footsteps of his father, they had a social worker with rage issues, a totally clueless Strider lupus and a red talon who constantly wanted to take over the pack. They imprisoned a Zmei, fought the remnants of Baba Yaga's armies, fought the Mob and its shadowy Tzimisce overlord and they even went up against the forces of the Weaver. But the big story, the one going through all of it was the Wendigo's dreams and nightmares... the ones that lead the pack halfway across the world to find the Siberakh and have them rejoin the Garou nation.<br /> <br /> My third game was done as a joke. We were going through Hengeyokai and we made characters as a lark. I was planning to run a session or two and maybe come back to it at a later time. Yeah... we kinda stopped playing two years later. We ended up fighting demons from hell, racing triads in souped up cars, cursing the fact that someone's mokole battle form was too big to use in buildings and fighting a wicked immortal sorceress that wanted to enslave the city of Hong Kong.<br /> <br /> Almost four years ago now, I've started an Ahadi campaign that's still going strong. We have a huge number of sessions, and due to a revolving cast and dangling plot threads, I'm actually running two concurrent plot threads in Tanzania and Egypt right now. I'm very happy with the marriage of the changing breeds, current politics, african mythology and the insanity the players have been up to. This game is probably the best demonstration of how much effect renown can have on the setting and how important the PC's can become to the setting at large... and how you really need to add extra conditions for characters to get Rank other then renown. Otherwise everyone would be rank 6 by now, rather then a solid 4 with strong political ties and plans to get into Rank 5. The group is actually responsible for founding at least 4 mixed packs that operate all over Africa.<br /> <br /> One of the things that thrills me the most about this game is how much I'm learning about the people, nature, mythology and history of Africa while doing prepwork for it. Plot highlights would include freeing the Bat of Africa and trying to revive his shifters, introducing Anansi as a patron to the Ananasi and fostering a schism among the spidrs, an Ajaba Death Metal band, saving a legendary Umbral Glenn of the Mokole from being taken by the Wyrm, saving the prince of Indian Simba and educating him among the Amadu, Daktari zombie action, breaking out Mubarak from the military prison and a bubasti seducing an immortal mummy nemesis of the Bubasti known as the Cat Swallower.<br /> <br /> The last, but not least is a shorter campaign I've been running over the last year and a half, staffed mostly by Werewolf newbies, about a Fianna Caern in Ireland, and a pack of young cubs learning the ropes and getting entangled in the business of scorned kinfolk, black spiral treachery and Balor One-Eye seeking to open the vast caves under Ireland and let out the Fomorians to conquer the world...<br /> <br /> <br /> If someone's interested I can tell you more about my games that worked out, and I've had a number of concepts sitting on the backburner waiting for better days. But, I'd really love to hear what you folks have been up to and what kind of games you've been running and playing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T06:57:52-08:00","id":753903,"title":"","content":"Where are you from ?<br /> <br /> <br /> I started Werewolf LARP around 1999. I have had played VtM as LARP and tabletop before, though. I have been playing every two months for one weekend ever since. So about 180 full LARP days. I have played werewolf tabletop a little, but no troupe really stayed together. The LARP however was one ongiong game all the time. And I become ST around 2009...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T08:18:53-08:00","id":754067,"title":"","content":"It all started way back in 1998, when two of my friends showed up at my door wanting to show me this awesome new card game they had gotten into: RAGE!<br /> I was really digging the lore behind the cards, and a few moths later I bought W:tA 2nd Edition.<br /> I ran a several sessions in 98-99, then nothing for a few years in the early 2000's following High School, and finally I'm about 15 sessions into a Wild West game I'm running right now.<br /> In that time I managed to play in a hand full of games, but nothing that went beyond a few sessions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/767-lostinsanity","name":"LostInSanity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T08:30:59-08:00","id":754077,"title":"","content":"I got my first WtA book (revised core), at Christmas 2004. From there, I collected books, but never properly played them.<br /> <br /> I started gaming proper 'round 2011. I've been into forum games, chat games, MUSH games and pretty much any format online has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T09:13:43-08:00","id":754148,"title":"","content":"I was introduced to the game in early 2005 and have been playing continuously (never been without at least one group) since then. We started with a mixed Fera group and played the characters every week for years on end, until the formerly newbish game had become much more mature, dark and the adventures of our characters were really second nature to us all. For me, it was &quot;that&quot; group that everyone has, that is so good that it sets the bar for everything that comes later. I'm running an online Ahadi game that has been going since 2006 and only ever missed one or two games, I've played via Team Speak for a while, and I also participated via video chat when I had to move away for my thesis but didn't want to leave my 'pack'. Considering how long the game exists, I'm late to the party but I tried my best to catch up on all the years I missed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/593/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3312-taci","name":"Taci","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3312_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T09:21:38-08:00","id":754161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taci</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/753855-so-how-much-experience-do-you-folks-have-with-werewolf?p=754148#post754148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was introduced to the game in early 2005 and have been playing continuously (never been without at least one group) since then. We started with a mixed Fera group and played the characters every week for years on end, until the formerly newbish game had become much more mature, dark and the adventures of our characters were really second nature to us all. For me, it was &quot;that&quot; group that everyone has, that is so good that it sets the bar for everything that comes later. I'm running an online Ahadi game that has been going since 2006 and only ever missed one or two games, I've played via Team Speak for a while, and I also participated via video chat when I had to move away for my thesis but didn't want to leave my 'pack'. Considering how long the game exists, I'm late to the party but I tried my best to catch up on all the years I missed.</div> </div> </div> </div>And then there is the art stuff too! I've noticed a lot of artistic WtA players draw. It has been fun sharing artworks on Deviantart, at least XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T09:57:49-08:00","id":754301,"title":"","content":"I was introduced to it after a disastrously abortive game of Vampire in 1996, in which the people running it didn't have the book and neglected to mention parts of character creation like Virtues and Willpower. After the day's game ended, I flipped through the Werewolf 1st edition player's guide, saw the Mokole and Rokea, and put Vampire away forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T12:08:49-08:00","id":754685,"title":"","content":"Saur Ops, I've had a friend showing me Vampire and totally going ga ga over their cool powers, and how the thing was awesome compared to D&amp;D. I liked it at start, on a very trenchcoat and katanas level. But the takeaway from the book was the writeup about the Lupines, with an amazing piece by Ron Spencer of a Werewolf murdering a vampire. That's when I knew I had to get it. Once I got my paws on Werewolf, I was hooked, and vampire was just so much dust in the wind.<br /> <br /> Everyone, thanks for pitching in. If you're up to it, I'd love to hear what kind of stories you ran, and what you've had the most fun with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8760,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","user":"Cogliostro","date":". 11-04-2015, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T12:15:25-08:00","id":754730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/753855-so-how-much-experience-do-you-folks-have-with-werewolf?p=754685#post754685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone, thanks for pitching in. If you're up to it, I'd love to hear what kind of stories you ran, and what you've had the most fun with?</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the first proper WtA games I ran was a Victorian Era tale of a legendary pack reborn. Very much a gray-morality one, because they allied with a BSD messiah to save China from the Opium Wars. Very silly, but I loved it.<br /> <br /> I've been in a lot of online games after that. One of my favourite stories was when a sept saved the world from a mega tainted Wyrm Incarna. Best of all was that it had an garou umbral navy and involved a lot of player actions.<br /> <br /> Second, and a more recent one, was when Weaver tainted Glass Walkers captured the kinfolk of a sept and experimented on them. The rescue was epic and fun, and I loved the whole usage of mechanical horror the STs used.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T12:23:18-08:00","id":754749,"title":"","content":"My group lacked focus and generally did Shadowrun. The rare occasions of anything from WW tended to have to make concessions toward some bizarre unified WoD vision because the people who introduced me to it had the unshakable conviction that all the games were meant to be together and took place in the same setting. It was a breath of fresh air when I read that no, this was not actually the intention as such and that stuff from outside of Werewolf didn't really matter to Werewolf. Of course, that wasn't going to fly with said group, which then saw a brief period of D&amp;D 3E, then Exalted, then my not really playing with them face to face, which was not really a big deal since life was going in separate directions anyway.<br /> <br /> We tried Under a Blood Red Moon, once. <i>Once</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T14:09:39-08:00","id":754897,"title":"","content":"I've ran some werewolf games (one was the darkness remembered larp at gen con one year)played in more. Not too big on vampire but it what my group likes to play, I'm more of a mage, dark heresy and shadow run guy though with a splash of pathfinder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T14:38:32-08:00","id":754972,"title":"","content":"I've never run Werewolf, only played it. I started with the first edition rulebook the day it came out in stores in 1992. I played LARP &quot;Laws of the Wyld&quot; for a few years in the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> I usually ran for my group - Transylvania Chronicles, Mage 2nd into Mage Revised, Exalted, Shadowrun, Feng Shui, Buffy. Aside from Mage and Exalted, and to a lesser extent, Transylvania Chronicles, those didn't last long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T14:48:52-08:00","id":754979,"title":"","content":"Heh, I was just curious about Werewolf mostly. I really didn't want to go in what else I've been running as I've got an absurd amount of different RPG's <span style=\"font-size:12px\">(CoC, Exalted, WoD, Laundry, Feng Shui, Trail of Cthulhu, all of Aeon, Fireborn, Dark heresy, Rogue Trader, Deathwatch, all forms of Deadlands, L5R, Ars Magica, 13th Age, Ravenloft, Shadowrun, Planesape, Eberron...)</span> but with Mage and Werewolf being closest to my heart <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T14:58:25-08:00","id":754992,"title":"","content":"I mostly went off into other stuff because I hadn't run Werewolf. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I've <i>played</i> Werewolf tabletop, but that was mostly a one-on-one game wherein I played a Ceilican so I hesitate to call it Were<i>wolf</i>. <br /> <br /> In LARP I played a couple of Ahroun and a Red Talon Philodox and people complained that my characters were too angry and violent or something. I mean I also played a Theurge and a Ragabash, so I wasn't just gravitating to angry (or angry-seeming) character concepts, just those particular characters seemed to bother people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T15:12:51-08:00","id":755010,"title":"","content":"Found a copy of the revised 2nd ed in the bargain bucket at my comics shop about... oh, 13 years ago, which at the time doubled as the FLGS, as someone who was at the time only dimly aware that RPG's other than D&amp;D existed it was like finding Excalibur in your sock draw. I ran the occasional game for my friends in school and played myself online through PbP's. It is to this day my favourite game of the OWoD and definately in my top 5 RPG's in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8485-random_interrupt","name":"Random_Interrupt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8485_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T18:54:46-08:00","id":755576,"title":"","content":"I bought first edition W:tA when the book first came out back in 1992. Unfortunately, I have had very few opportunities to play it over the years. I've lived most of my life in a small town where finding a game of D&amp;D was often hard, much less Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T09:04:13-08:00","id":756653,"title":"","content":"Started with Werewolf when it was my turn to run a game, that was 2nd edition. <br /> <br /> The longest running chronicle I ran was called &quot;Suffer the Children&quot; it started as a one shot story when two of my gaming group showed up at my house on a Saturday night. That particular chronicle started with a human trafficking ring selling a kinfolk child at auction in New Orleans. Moved to Denver to find the sold kinfolk, which led to a child pornography ring. Moved to a school/orphanage in Kansas based in part on Milton Hershey School. Then to California to confront a former student who was active in denying that child pornography was harmful. Then to Nevada and a dying town where the players finally found the address for the mastermind which led to Maine after a narrow escape the players tracked him to the Caribbean sea, but missed him. The chronicle ended in the Canary islands and the Wyrm ruins. The chronicle ran for almost 3 years. The only two characters that survived the entire story were a Red Talon Ragabash and a Black Fury Ahroun. And both had a number of battle scars. <br /> <br /> Through the Ages was my next chronicle that one ran as long but was a generational story. Each story in the chronicle ran with descendants from the first story and centered on a Caern on an island in the Adriatic Sea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T02:27:44-08:00","id":760577,"title":"","content":"Shit, I just realized I've played for nearly 20 years now - thanks for making me feel like an old man...<br /> <br /> So - my experience so far... I got introduced to VtM, but got extremely curious after a werewolf-pack was introduced as antagonists. It took 3 months of nagging at the storyteller before he finally prepared &quot;a proper game&quot; for us, and it was love at first sight for me. The group all liked werewolf so much that we stuck with it through the years, and even though we occasionally flirted with other games, we always came back to WtA.<br /> <br /> I've been a player in only two games, and had 6 chronicles of my own. The two chronicles I've played in myself was modern age New York (college-game over a span of 6 months with a new ST who had to cut his teeth as ST) and Portland (the first werewolf-game I played, we kept the chronicle going for almost four years).<br /> <br /> The games I've run myself are:<br /> Dark Ages (The early forming of England, 880-900 AD), where we ran 2 groups at the same time - combined this lasted for three years, where downtime for one pack meant activity for the other.<br /> <br /> In modern ages I had a two-year chronicle set in Appalachia, a four-year chronicle set in Indianapolis (my first and longest-running chronicle to date), a two-year chronicle in Morocco/North Africa (where I successfully adopted a dual-ST-system, where a friend of mine sat in and co-ran the game with me - this is highly recommended, by the way), a short 6-month-chronicle in Chicago and my current game that takes place in modern-day Balkans (Mainly in Mirovice, Kosovo).<br /> <br /> I like to look for interesting places and historical eras to set my games in, and I go out of my way to place the players outside of their comfort zones any way I can. I also try to make my games as cruel and unforgiving as the world of darkness can be at it's worst, and I'm actually rather surprised that only one of my players have thrown in the towel this far.<br /> <br /> I have the privilege to play with veterans, great roleplayers and friends that have been with me since the very beginning - they are a solid group that finds their way to the table week after week, year after year. And we enjoy it just as much as we did 20 years ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9021-jeremiah-songkeeper","name":"Jeremiah Songkeeper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}